@startuml TestExecution_Flow
title Test Execution Flow - TDD Cycle

start

:Developer writes test case;
note right
  RED Phase
  Test fails because
  implementation doesn't exist
end note

:Run test;
if (Test passes?) then (No)
    :Continue to GREEN phase;
else (Yes)
    :Test already passing?;
    stop
endif

:Write minimal implementation;
note right
  GREEN Phase
  Write just enough code
  to make test pass
end note

:Run test;
if (Test passes?) then (Yes)
    :Continue to REFACTOR phase;
else (No)
    :Fix implementation;
    :Go back to run test;
endif

:Refactor code;
note right
  REFACTOR Phase
  Improve code quality
  while keeping tests passing
end note

:Run test;
if (Test passes?) then (Yes)
    :Continue;
else (No)
    :Fix refactored code;
    :Go back to run test;
endif

:Run all tests;
if (All tests pass?) then (Yes)
    :Code review;
else (No)
    :Fix failing tests;
    :Go back to run all tests;
endif

:Commit code;
:Push to repository;

:CI/CD pipeline runs;
note right
  - Build
  - Run all tests
  - Code coverage
  - SonarQube analysis
end note

if (Pipeline passes?) then (Yes)
    :Deploy to Dev environment;
else (No)
    :Fix issues;
    :Push again;
endif

:Write next test case;
:Go back to start;

@enduml
